---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import StatusCodeLookup from '../../components/StatusCodeLookup.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="HTTP Status Code Lookup"
  description="Search HTTP status codes by number or keyword and get a plain-English explanation of what caused it and what to do."
>
  <StatusCodeLookup client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why a searchable lookup helps</h2>
  <p>
    Remembering the exact meaning of every HTTP status code isn't practical
    — this tool lets you search by number (like "429") or by keyword (like
    "rate limit" or "unauthorized") to instantly find the right code and
    understand what it means for your API integration.
  </p>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>What's the difference between 401 and 403?</strong> 401 means
    you're not authenticated at all (no valid credentials), while 403 means
    you are authenticated but don't have permission for this specific
    resource.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Should I retry on a 5xx error?</strong> Generally yes, with
    exponential backoff — 5xx errors usually indicate a temporary server-side
    issue, unlike 4xx errors which mean your request itself needs fixing.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
